Relationships:
-------------
MFE_CoreEngine --> MFE_PositiveFlux     (creates +flux)
MFE_CoreEngine --> MFE_NegativeFlux     (creates -flux)
MFE_CoreEngine --> MFE_Coupling         (applies coupling rules)
MFE_CoreEngine --> MFE_FluxLoop         (executes bipolar flux loop)

MFE_PositiveFlux <--> MFE_NegativeFlux  (bipolar symmetry)
MFE_Coupling --> MFE_FluxLoop           (modulates oscillation)
MFE_FluxLoop --> RDG_State              (writes flux into relational geometry)

Notes:
------
* MFE_PositiveFlux and MFE_NegativeFlux form a bipolar pair.
* MFE_Coupling defines how the fluxes interact.
* MFE_FluxLoop stabilizes or oscillates flux based on coupling.
* MFE_CoreEngine orchestrates the entire flux cycle.
* Output is written into RDG_State for downstream Q and RME processing.
